1
00:00:00,402 --> 00:00:02,572
(Howard:)And you love the sound
of your own voice.

2
00:00:02,571 --> 00:00:04,341
(Sheldon:)Yeah, well, of course I do.

3
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:05,510
(Sheldon:)Listen to it.

4
00:00:05,507 --> 00:00:08,777
(Sheldon:)It's like an earful
of melted caramel.

5
00:00:08,777 --> 00:00:11,047
(Leonard:)Look, most importantly,

6
00:00:11,046 --> 00:00:13,716
(Leonard:)this will let you move on
and study dark matter.

7
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:17,750
(Sheldon:)It is true that many of
my heroes have taken students

8
00:00:17,753 --> 00:00:19,023
under their wings:

9
00:00:19,021 --> 00:00:22,361
(Sheldon:)Feynman, Einstein, Professor X.

10
00:00:22,358 --> 00:00:24,858
(Sheldon:)Humorously,

11
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:26,430
(Sheldon:)in the case of Professor X,

12
00:00:26,428 --> 00:00:28,698
(Sheldon:)some of his students
actually had wings.

13
00:00:28,697 --> 00:00:30,897
(Sheldon:)That's rich.

14
00:00:32,301 --> 00:00:34,231
(Sheldon:)I'll use that one
to lighten the mood

15
00:00:34,236 --> 00:00:37,136
(Sheldon:)after my entire class
fails the midterm.

16
00:00:40,843 --> 00:00:44,073
(Amy:)Measuring starfish
serotonin levels in response

17
00:00:44,079 --> 00:00:47,979
(Amy:)to one point two molar
stimulation of pleasure cells.

18
00:00:49,919 --> 00:00:52,819
(Amy:)You like that, don't you?

19
00:00:52,821 --> 00:00:54,621
(Amy:)That's right, say my name.

20
00:00:54,623 --> 00:00:58,393
(Skype ringtone playing)

